# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Literature Wiki — frontend environment
# Copy to `.env.local` and edit. All NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars are inlined at BUILD time.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Site identity (branding) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shown in the browser tab, top nav brand, sidebar, and chat welcome.
# These NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars are baked into the bundle at `pnpm build` time, so set
# them BEFORE building — changing them at `pnpm start` runtime has no effect.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_TITLE="QSGE Literature Wiki"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_DESCRIPTION="Quantitative Spatial General Equilibrium knowledge base — from classical spatial economics to dynamic frontier extensions, with a focus on Chinese applications."
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_GREETING="Ask the QSGE wiki…"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_PLACEHOLDER="Search the spatial economics literature…"

# ── RAG backend (Chat surface only) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Chat (/) talks to the FastAPI backend (../rag/server.py). Browse and Search do
# NOT need the backend.
#
# API base resolution order:
#   1. NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL — explicit absolute override.
#   2. else (in browser) <page-host>:<NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_PORT>  (LAN/ZeroTier friendly).
#   3. else http://localhost:<NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_PORT>          (SSR fallback).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL="http://localhost:8000"
NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_PORT="8000"

# ── Wiki content directory (Browse + View surfaces) ──────────────────────────
# Server-side filesystem path to the wiki markdown layer, relative to web/ (or
# absolute). Browse (/wiki) and View (/wiki/[slug]) read *.md from here directly,
# so they work with NO backend. Default: ../wiki
#   • Template demo:  WIKI_DIR=../examples/demo-wiki/wiki
WIKI_DIR="../wiki"
